From 70609e7452e3223de4ca034439cafb55961c93e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 19:36:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.5.0a: remove bundled tcpdump packet-capture; harden
 AI Advisor diagnostics

- Remove the Network Tools "Packet Capture" page and the bundled tcpdump build
  (RTCONFIG_TCPDUMP off): drops a large legacy dependency and its attack surface.
  Users who need packet capture can install tcpdump via Entware.
- AI Advisor network-diagnostics hardening (rmcpd): stricter probe-target
  validation (block IPv6 loopback/link-local/ULA and extra reserved IPv4 ranges),
  reject option-shaped DNS names, validate the LAN interface name before use,
  and clean up the single-flight diagnostic lock.
- reaper_mcp.cgi: require the router http_id token on state-changing actions
  (CSRF hardening).
- rtrafd: JSON-escape emitted string fields; clamp the monthly-quota math.

Both variants (MCP + noMCP).
